 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Route rules are recorded on the bundle at decoration time and replayed onto the app when the bundle is registered.\n\n1. **Record (decoration time).** `Bundle.attach_route_rule()` in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413` doesn't touch an app. It calls `Bundle.record()` (`bundles.py:224`) with a lambda that calls `state.attach_route_rule(...)`. The lambda is appended to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n2. **Register.** `Tessel.register_bundle()` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571` calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (`bundles.py:273`, called at `app.py:596`).\n3. **Setup state.** `Bundle.register()` calls `Bundle.make_setup_state()` (`bundles.py:246`), which returns a `BundleSetupState` (`bundles.py:41`). That state resolves `url_prefix`, `subdomain`, `url_defaults` and the name prefix from the registration options or the bundle's own values.\n4. **Replay.** `Bundle.register()` loops over `self.deferred_functions` and calls each one with the state (`bundles.py:334-335`). It also adds the bundle's static route through `state.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:323-328`).\n5. **Apply to the app.** `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule()` (`bundles.py:87`) does three things:\n   - prepends `url_prefix` to the rule;\n   - sets the subdomain and merges the defaults;\n   - prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.` and calls `app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`bundles.py:110`).\n6. **Nested bundles.** The end of `register()` (`bundles.py:349-377`) recursively registers child bundles. It combines the parent's `url_prefix` and `subdomain` into the child's options first.\n\n`Bundle._merge_bundle_funcs()` (`bundles.py:379`) copies the bundle's `view_functions`, error handlers and request hooks into the app, but the URL rules themselves go through the deferred `attach_route_rule` path.",
